        en: "Senja Berg from the Swedish Prosecution Authority telephoned the Stockholm office at 07:05. She has an encrypted package seized under a Swedish intercept order and she wants Laplace to open it. Her written request is in your inbox, along with a note from Legal and one from the Americans.\n\nAxiom Stockholm will not decide this. I will not decide it from Zürich either. You are the closest person with the clearance, so it is your call, and it has to be a call rather than a shrug.\n\nRead the request and the legal note, then decide whether we assist. If you take it, the package is on the secure terminal in the Monitor app. If you decline, decline in writing, on the record, with a reason a court could read. Either way, mail me your decision before you leave for the airport. If you open the terminal and cannot finish, abandon the package rather than leaving it half-decrypted: a partial decrypt is worse than a refusal, because it looks like we tried and failed.\n\nI do not care about the American angle. The Americans will call you; they always do. What matters is that a prosecutor asked in writing and that we answer in writing.\n\nZoe\n\nSent from my phone. Do not forward.",
        zh: "Swedish 检察署的 Senja Berg 今早 07:05 给 Stockholm 办公室打了电话。她手上有一个依据 Swedish 截获令扣押的加密包裹，想让 Laplace 打开。她的书面请求在你的收件箱里，另外还有法务的一份说明和 Americans 的一份来函。\n\nAxiom Stockholm 不会做这个决定。我也不会在 Zürich 替你们做。你是最近、且有权限的人，所以这由你决定——而且必须是一个决定，不是一个耸肩。\n\n读完请求和法务意见，再决定我们是否协助。如果接手，包裹在 Monitor app 的安全终端上。如果拒绝，就书面拒绝、留档、给出一个法院能读的理由。无论哪种，在你去机场之前把决定发给我。如果你打开了终端却做不完，就放弃包裹，不要留一个半解密的残件：半解密比拒绝更糟，因为它看起来像是我们试过并且失败了。\n\n我不在乎 Americans 那一边。他们一定会打给你，他们总是会。要紧的是：检察官书面提出了请求，而我们书面回答。\n\nZoe\n\n发自手机。请勿转发。"
