      time: "08:50",
      date: "2027-02-17",
      body: {
        en: "Axiom is under no legal obligation to assist a Swedish prosecutor with a decryption request. That is the short answer. The rest is the part you should read before you decide.\n\nIf we assist, we act as a technical service provider to the prosecution. Scope should be limited in writing to this package and this case reference. Recovered data should be handed to the prosecutor and not retained. That is Axiom's exposure under Swedish law, and it is manageable.\n\nThere are two other exposures. The first is diplomatic: the Embassy of Iran has written to us and will argue that the material is protected diplomatic correspondence. I will not tell you that argument is correct; I will tell you that it will be made publicly if this becomes known. The second is political: the United States will want the result, and the United States is not a party to this request.\n\nMy advice: no obligation, no prohibition, and no appetite in this department for being the reason it happened. The decision belongs to you and Zoe. If you assist, keep it to the eight values and the package, and log the request. If you refuse, refuse in writing to the prosecutor and copy me.\n\nNadine Keller\nSenior Counsel, Axiom Legal",
        zh: "Axiom 没有法律义务协助 Swedish 检察官的解密请求。这是简短的回答。其余部分，是你做决定之前该读的。\n\n如果协助，我们是检察署的技术服务提供方。范围应以书面限定在这个数据包和这个案号。恢复的数据应交给检察官，不得留存。这是 Axiom 在 Swedish 法律下的风险，可控。\n\n另外还有两重风险。第一是外交：Iran 使馆已来信，会主张该材料属于受保护的外交通信。我不会告诉你这个主张是对的；我会告诉你，一旦事情公开，这个主张一定会被公开提出。第二是政治：Americans 会想要结果，而 Americans 并不是这项请求的当事方。\n\n我的意见：没有义务，没有禁止，本部门也没有兴趣成为事情发生的原因。决定权在你和 Zoe。若协助，只做那八个数值和数据包，并记录请求；若拒绝，就书面拒绝检察官并抄送我。\n\nNadine Keller\nAxiom Legal 高级法律顾问"
      }
