      attachments: ["f_alan_note"],
      body: {
        en: "Dear colleague,\n\nThe Swedish request is not as confidential as you might assume. I am the Counsellor for Political Affairs at the U.S. Embassy in Bern, and I have read a summary of the package. It concerns a matter in which the United States has an interest, and the Swedish authorities know that we have an interest.\n\nAxiom Dynamics is an American company. I do not need to explain what that means in practice, and I would rather not put it in a letter. When a request of this kind is made of a company with American roots, we expect the company to cooperate with us as well as with the Swedish prosecutor, and to share what it recovers as a matter of course.\n\nI am not asking you to break Swedish law. I am telling you that this file will be read in Washington, and that the difference between a helpful company and an unhelpful one is usually one conversation.\n\nYou can reach me on this address, or on the number below.\n\nAlan Hart\nCounsellor for Political Affairs\nU.S. Embassy Bern\n+41 31 555 01 20",
        zh: "同事你好：\n\nSwedish 的这项请求并没有你想的那么保密。我是 U.S. Embassy Bern 的政治事务参赞，已经读过包裹的摘要。它涉及 Americans 有利益的事项，而 Swedish 当局知道我们有利益。\n\nAxiom Dynamics 是一家 American 公司。我不需要解释这在实践中意味着什么，也不愿意把它写进信里。当这样一份请求递到一家有 American 根基的公司面前，我们期待它与 Swedish 检察官合作的同时也与我们一起合作，并按惯例分享它恢复出来的东西。\n\n我不是在要求你违反 Swedish 法律。我是在告诉你，这份文件会被 Washington 读到；而一家有帮助的公司和一家没有帮助的公司，区别通常只是一次谈话。\n\n你可以通过这个邮箱或下面的号码联系我。\n\nAlan Hart\n政治事务参赞\nU.S. Embassy Bern\n+41 31 555 01 20"
      }
